Build with GCC 15: its C23 default reads an empty parameter list as (void), and GMP's configure compiler test declares g() that way and calls it with six arguments, so it decides there is no working compiler.

--- a/PKGBUILD
+++ b/PKGBUILD
@@ -20,4 +20,6 @@
 build() {
   export CC="gcc -m32"
   export CXX="g++ -m32"
+  # GCC 15 defaults to C23: GMP's configure tests need gnu17
+  export CFLAGS+=" -std=gnu17"
   export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="/usr/lib32/pkgconfig"
